diagnostic_evidence.quote:
Reparametrization by the scalar state.
Define
\begin{align}
    \delta := \frac{4\, a_*^2}{a_*^4 + 1}.
    \label{eq:appendix_delta_from_astar}
\end{align}

failure_location.quote:
Then $P(\delta)$ is uniquely determined for every $\delta \in [\delta_{\mathrm{th}}(\eta), \overline\delta)$. With state space $(0, 2]$, the unique family is
\begin{align}
    P(\delta)
    = \frac{1}{4 - \delta^2}
    \begin{pmatrix}
        \delta & -\delta^2/2 \\
        -\delta^2/2 & \delta
    \end{pmatrix},
\end{align}
